# Shell scripts must keep LF endings.
#
# build.sh is executed by Vercel's Linux build image. A CRLF checkout makes
# bash fail immediately with "\r: command not found" on the shebang. This
# machine has core.autocrlf=true and previously had no attributes at all, so
# the working copy was CRLF while the blob happened to stay LF — correct by
# accident, not by rule. Pin it so a Windows checkout cannot break the build.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Rules and config deployed as-is; keep byte-exact line endings.
*.json text eol=lf
*.mjs text eol=lf
